From: Simon Polack <spolack+git@mailbox.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:22:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Ethernet: W5500 over SPI

A new Ethernet board type, "W5500 (SPI)" (WLED_ETH_W5500), for boards
with a W5500 instead of an RMII PHY. It needs a core with the W5500
driver (CONFIG_ETH_SPI_ETHERNET_W5500, as Arduino core 3 has for the
ESP32); without, choosing it only logs that. Pins are build flags
(WLED_W5500_SCLK/MISO/MOSI/CS/INT/RST, default VSPI with CS 5 and INT 4)
plus WLED_W5500_OE, an active-low output enable driven low (e.g. a level
shifter that also carries the LED outputs).

Only its own pins are reserved: the RMII pins (19, 21, 22, 25, 26, 27)
stay free, as they are often LED outputs or I2C on such boards. The pins
of the selected board are listed in one place (ethernetPins), used for
the pin reservation report and the configuration.
